  "notes": "{分離|ぶんり} is a formal term for separating or isolating things that were previously joined or mixed. Used across many fields: science, politics, medicine, and engineering.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {政教|せいきょう}{分離|ぶんり}: separation of church and state\n- {分離|ぶんり}{独立|どくりつ}: secession, separatist independence\n- {分離|ぶんり}{手術|しゅじゅつ}: separation surgery (e.g., conjoined twins)\n- {分離|ぶんり}する: to separate, to isolate\n- {分離|ぶんり}される: to be separated\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {分割|ぶんかつ}: division (into parts or portions)\n- {分裂|ぶんれつ}: splitting, fission (often irreversible)\n- {隔離|かくり}: isolation, quarantine (especially of people)\n- {離脱|りだつ}: withdrawal, secession (from a group)\n\nUSAGE:\nAs a する verb, both transitive and intransitive uses are possible: AをBから{分離|ぶんり}する (to separate A from B) or AがBから{分離|ぶんり}する (A separates from B).",
